1
00:00:00,040 --> 00:00:04,110
Next on our list is to take a walk around York museum gardens.
清单上的下一项，是在约克博物馆花园里散散步。

2
00:00:04,120 --> 00:00:10,480
These botanical gardens are a peaceful oasis in the center of York and we find they make a really nice break from the crowded streets.
这些植物园是约克市中心一片宁静的绿洲，我们觉得，在这里能很好地暂时远离拥挤的街道。

3
00:00:10,480 --> 00:00:18,160
As well as being well maintained free to enter and beautiful all year round the gardens are also home to the ruins of saint mary's abbey.
这些花园养护得很好，免费开放，而且一年四季都很美；除此之外，这里还有圣玛丽修道院的遗址。

4
00:00:18,160 --> 00:00:23,620
The abbey was first built in 1088 by william the conqueror and was once the richest abbey in northern England.
据作者介绍，这座修道院最初由征服者威廉于一〇八八年建造，曾是英格兰北部最富有的修道院。

5
00:00:23,620 --> 00:00:30,939
However as Henry viii dissolved monasteries throughout the country saint mary's abbey like so many others fell into disrepair.
然而，随着亨利八世在全国解散修道院，圣玛丽修道院也像许多其他修道院一样，逐渐失修。

6
00:00:30,939 --> 00:00:40,470
These incredible ruins are now a highlight of the gardens and you should try to factor some time into your trip to take a stroll here especially if the weather is on your side.
如今，这些壮观的遗址是花园的一大亮点；作者建议旅行时留些时间来这里散步，尤其是天气也帮忙的时候。

7
00:00:40,480 --> 00:00:46,650
York previously renamed jorvik was first invaded by the vikings in the year 866.
约克曾被改称 Jorvik；据这段介绍，维京人首次入侵约克是在八六六年。

8
00:00:46,660 --> 00:00:49,780
They settled in and ruled over the city for around a century.
他们在这里定居下来，统治这座城市约一个世纪。

9
00:00:49,780 --> 00:00:57,520
If you're interested in learning more about viking history archeology and what viking life would have been like then you can visit jorvik viking center.
如果你想进一步了解维京历史、考古，以及当年的维京生活可能是什么样，就可以去 Jorvik 维京中心。

10
00:00:57,520 --> 00:01:05,680
I haven't been since I was a child but to this day I can still remember the dark ride which takes you through the sights sounds and smells of a replica viking village.
我从小孩子的时候去过之后，就再也没去过，但直到今天，我仍记得那个室内乘车游览项目：它带你感受一个复原维京村庄的景象、声音和气味。

11
00:01:05,680 --> 00:01:11,910
So while we can't say how good it is for an adult's only trip I can vouch for it being a memorable experience for kids.
所以，虽然我们说不准只有成年人去玩会有多好，但我可以保证，这会是孩子们难忘的体验。

12
00:01:11,920 --> 00:01:17,620
Near York train station is the national railway museum which is the largest museum of its kind in the country.
约克火车站附近就是国家铁路博物馆，据作者介绍，它是英国同类博物馆中规模最大的。

13
00:01:17,620 --> 00:01:24,220
Even as someone who isn't particularly interested in trains I still thought this was a fantastic attraction in York and well worth visiting.
即使我这个对火车并不是特别感兴趣的人，也仍然觉得这是约克一个很棒的景点，非常值得一看。

14
00:01:24,220 --> 00:01:29,620
The museum has a huge collection of locomotives of various types from different periods in history.
博物馆收藏了大量来自不同历史时期、各种类型的机车。

15
00:01:30,100 --> 00:01:36,999
I particularly enjoyed being able to peer inside the royal carriages walk through the 1970 s shinkansen otherwise known as the bullet train.
我尤其喜欢能向皇家车厢里探看，走进那列一九七〇年代的新干线，也就是人们所说的子弹头列车。

16
00:01:36,999 --> 00:01:40,300
And being able to actually walk underneath one of the locomotives.
我也很喜欢竟然能走到其中一台机车的下方去看。

17
00:01:40,300 --> 00:01:47,559
The museum is free to enter with a suggested donation and is open from 10 am until 5 or 6 pm depending on the time of year.
作者说，这家博物馆免费入场，建议自愿捐款；上午十点开放，到下午五点或六点关门，具体取决于一年中的时段。

18
00:01:47,559 --> 00:01:52,830
We both really enjoyed this museum and would recommend popping in if you can.
我们俩都很喜欢这家博物馆，如果有机会，建议你进去看看。

19
00:01:52,840 --> 00:01:57,999
Take a stroll down the paved banks of the picturesque river ouse and watch the birds and the boaters go by.
沿着风景如画的乌斯河铺砌好的河岸散步，看鸟儿与划船的人从身边经过。

20
00:01:57,999 --> 00:02:01,840
If you like you can join the short cruise on an open deck sightseeing boat.
如果愿意，你可以参加一趟短途游船，乘坐露天甲板观光船。

21
00:02:01,840 --> 00:02:07,590
Or if you would rather do the driving yourself you can hire a small boat for up to one hour.
或者，如果你更想自己驾驶，也可以租一艘小船，最长租用一小时。

22
00:02:07,600 --> 00:02:11,800
If you like a good street name then you'll love spotting some of the names of the streets in York.
如果你喜欢有趣的街名，就一定会喜欢留意约克这些街道的名字。

23
00:02:11,800 --> 00:02:17,499
The most famous and most peculiar is whip ma whop ma gate this is the shortest route in York.
其中最有名、也最奇特的是 Whip-Ma-Whop-Ma-Gate。作者说，这是约克最短的一条路。

24
00:02:17,499 --> 00:02:22,890
And in 1505 was known as whitnourwhatnourgate which translated to what a street.
并且，据这段旁白所说，一五〇五年它曾叫 Whitnourwhatnourgate，作者把它解释成“真是一条街啊”。

25
00:02:22,900 --> 00:02:29,500
The more eagle eyed among you may notice when walking around York that there are small cat statues dotted around various buildings.
眼尖的朋友在约克四处走动时，可能会注意到，一些小猫雕像零星分布在各式建筑上。

26
00:02:30,040 --> 00:02:38,140
It is thought that originally cat statues were placed on buildings to ward away evil spirits and to frighten away rats which carried the plague and other illnesses.
据说，最初人们把猫雕像放在建筑上，是为了驱走邪灵，也为了吓跑那些会传播瘟疫及其他疾病的老鼠。

27
00:02:38,740 --> 00:02:43,300
A fun and free activity is to pick up a map from York glass located on the Shambles.
作者推荐的一项有趣又免费的活动，是到位于肉铺街的 York Glass 领一张地图。

28
00:02:43,300 --> 00:02:48,180
Or download the map to your phone and follow the trail trying to spot the different cats hidden around the city.
或者把地图下载到手机上，沿着小径走，试着找到藏在城里不同地方的那些猫雕像。

29
00:02:48,180 --> 00:02:52,420
If you do have time for a day trip from York then we would recommend Yorkshire air museum.
如果你确实有时间从约克出发来一趟一日游，那么我们会推荐约克郡航空博物馆。

30
00:02:52,420 --> 00:02:56,800
Today it is one of the largest independent aviation museums in the country.
在作者录制这段视频时，它是英国规模最大的独立航空博物馆之一。

31
00:02:56,800 --> 00:03:03,280
And houses historic aircrafts vehicles and fascinating exhibits within restored original world war ii buildings.
它还在经过修复的二战时期原有建筑内，收藏了历史飞机、车辆和引人入胜的展品。
